we've been talking a lot about Bernie  Sanders lately we've been talking a lot  about Joe Biden and how he fits into the  2020 Democratic primary we talked  yesterday on the bonus show about how  Beto O'Rourke has almost totally  disappeared from media coverage and his  polling is down as well from the 8 to 12  range Beto is down to as low as 3% in  two recent polls but what about  Elizabeth Warren Warren is doing some  really good stuff Warren is not only  starting to get some headway and  positive feedback in magic ountry at the  events that she's been holding she's  also pushed into the double digits in a  lot of recent polls and she's not doing  it with flash or charisma because as  I've said before I don't find her  particularly rife with charisma or  relatability but she's doing it with  policy proposals that are really  interesting many of which makes sense  now first of all lots of right-wingers  have been skeptical of Warren as some  kind of anti business anti  entrepreneurship type and she's really  not so when she shows up and talks about  letting entrepreneurs and markets work  in a controlled way that actually is  having some appeal across party lines  but she also has some really specific  and solid proposals that are strongly  socially Democratic and this is a lot of  the stuff I've been talking about for  years so let's look at some examples of  Elizabeth Warren's really great policy  proposals number one antitrust Elizabeth  Warren wants to pass legislation that  will require large tech platforms be  designated as platform utilities and get  broken apart or separated from  participants on that platform  she also as part of her antitrust ideas  would appoint regulators committed to  reversing illegal and anti-competitive  tech mergers really important and she  talks about protecting the future of the  Internet which is of course the  importance of net neutrality really  great stuff and I'm completely behind it  she's also proposed an ultra millionaire  tax and this would be a wealth tax on  the richest Americans and it would apply  to households with a net worth of over  50 million dollars so this is only about  75 households in a country of 300 and  million people it's the top 0.1% the way  it would work is you pay a two percent  tax on every dollar of net worth above  50 million dollars and a three percent  tax on every dollar of net worth above a  billion this is expected to raise nearly  three trillion dollars over a 10-year  period now I do have a concern about  this I'm unsure about this proposal but  it's a specific proposal and I think it  is fantastic that Elizabeth Warren is  talking really specifically my concern  about the wealth tax is that a lot of  that net worth that people have on paper  is not liquid and I don't think it would  be a good idea to enforce a tax that  might require rich people to sell assets  in order to pay the wealth tax and  that's just kind of like a question mark  for me I also have other questions about  whether we should be focused on wealth  or maybe looking at capital gains more  importantly but it doesn't matter right  like my exact opinion on this idea  doesn't matter this is a very specific  and ambitious proposal universal child  care the universal childcare proposal  that Elizabeth Warren has put out there  would see the government partner with  local childcare providers and childcare  would be free to anyone who is at 200%  of the federal poverty line or below and  then if you are above 200% of the  federal poverty line the cost of child  care would be capped at 7% of income it  would be paid for by the old for  millionaire tax that I just told you  about very interesting and important  proposal and there are positive  externalities of freeing up people to go  and work and earn wages that are good  for the government and they're good for  those families and it's a really  interesting proposal Elizabeth Warren  has a housing investment plan which she  says will bring down rental costs by 10%  over ten years and create a million and  a half jobs in construction and  renovation it would see the government  invest five hundred billion over the  next ten years to build preserve and  preserve and renovate units of housing  units which will be affordable to low  income families  textbook social democracy and she would  pay for it by a tweak to the estate tax  this is another very good proposal from  Elizabeth Warren you may remember that  when George W Bush was in office the  first seven million of an estate were  exempt from taxes that has been raised  to twenty-two million dollars Elizabeth  Warren would simply lower it back to  seven million dollars and also tweak  some of the numbers in terms of the  estate tax rates for people who have  really really big estates I could go on  there's many more of these proposals but  this is a sampling and what is really  important to understand about this is  that Elizabeth Warren is not changing  the capitalist system that we have she's  allowing entrepreneurship she's allowing  business she's allowing people to get  very rich and all of that stuff but  she's saying we're gonna use some of  that money to keep people from being  left behind we're gonna have relatively  modest government involvement a little  more in line with some of those Nordic  and Scandinavian economies and these are  serious specific proposals that go way  beyond what many other candidates are  doing or talking about so this is a  substance over style approach it may not  work right I mean she's polling third or  fourth depending on the poll that you  look at at a certain point if she's  going to be the nominee she needs to  start making more headway than she has  and I don't know that this substance  over style approach will actually appeal  to enough people Biden's for about  polling 40% and he's so far has been  running almost exclusively on Trump is  bad and I will defeat him which I've  pointed out is not a great way to run a  campaign Bernie on the other hand is  more in line with the progressive ideas  that people are actually looking for  when they are pulled fairly about what  they think government should be doing  and he's polling 14 to 18 percent  depending on the poll and Warren is  putting out detailed policy proposals  that make a lot of sense  and she's polling like 7 to 12 so I  don't know  that substance over style is gonna get  you the nomination I don't know that if  it gets you the nomination that it will  get you the presidency very depressing  unfortunately but really great that  Elizabeth Warren is doing this and it is  appealing to some voters who are taking  the time to go to her town hall events  and listen to what she has to say let me  know what you think about her proposals  about this approach the show is on  Instagram at David Pakman show
 

